WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.040
<b>Let Me Introduce My Crazy 
Colleagues in This Bookstore!</b>

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:08.660
<i>No books are published 
during the long holiday,</i>

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.280
<i>so they get released the days before.</i>

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.670
<i>Please think...</i>

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.160
<i>of the bookstores!</i>

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.500
The new books haven't arrived, right?

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.130
Right?!

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.120
Thank goodness!

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.660
Our books are at the bottom!

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.680
Don't pack those yet! We have sheets!

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.530
Close one, thanks!

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.370
I haven't stocked a single shelf yet.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.340
I'll do it tomorrow.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.070
The packing machine's dead! 
I can't prep for tomorrow!

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:36.760
I wanna go home!

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.310
<b>All these books need to be put on display</b>

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:37.790
Denied!

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:44.350
<i>***Monogatari</i> keeps disappearing 
from the shelves!

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:50.850
<i>You there, who wanted to work at 
a bookstore after seeing Episode 1...</i>

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.850
<i>Thanks, but reconsider!</i>

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.760
Hey, no negative campaigning!

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.920
<b>Putting out the books that go on sale today</b>

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.080
Here's <i>*jin</i>.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.090
Here's <i>**tan</i>.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.470
Put them out. Put them out!

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.260
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.230
<b>Opening. Sorting / Cashier</b>

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:06.100
There's no end to the sorting!

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.470
What the hell is with all these books?!

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:09.160
Hello.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.160
Thank you for waiting!

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.280
Thank you.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.090
Hello.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.280
Thank you.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.040
Hello.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.010
<b>Prepping the afternoon shipment & 
for new books arriving the next day</b>

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.310
I want to go home.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.660
<i>Here's an important point to make:</i>

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.390
<i>The timing at which the 
books are put on display.</i>

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.490
<i>There are two kinds of Japanese comics.</i>

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.660
<b>Magazine-type comics</b>

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.660
<b>Book-type comics</b>

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:33.600
<i>The book-type comics, which need to be 
put on display as soon as they arrive.</i>

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:39.130
<b>Book-type comics</b>

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:39.130
<b>Put on display immediately 
upon arrival. Often arrives around 
five days before official release date.</b>

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.830
<i>These often arrive about five days before
 official release, so we have to be careful.</i>

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:42.170
<i>And then there are the magazine-type 
books, which have strict release dates.</i>

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:48.340
<b>Magazine-type comics</b>

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:48.340
<b>If you put these on display before release, 
you'll get the shit beaten out of you.</b>

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:45.800
<i>If we were to ever put them on 
display before their release dates,</i>

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.670
<i>we'd probably get the shit kicked 
out of us by a bunch of folks.</i>

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.010
<b>There has to be a better way to say this</b>

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.780
The new-release books are coming.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.040
Don't worry, it's fine!

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:56.880
We can do it!

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.570
Guys, there isn't a single copy 
of <i>Young M**azine</i> out front!

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.890
Do we have any stock?

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.320
Second column from the right, 
third row from the back.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.890
Sweet! Thanks!

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.270
Dammit, I'm stuck.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.330
Honda-san, could you add these
 to the new books table?!

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.660
What the hell?! It's like 
you're being tortured!

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:11.300
Found it!

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.830
Honda! Let's do the <i>Young 
M***zine</i> when you get back!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.900
Got it.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.060
Pardon me!

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.610
Pardon me!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.020
Pardon—

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.110
<b>Mega lineup</b>

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.750
Hello.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.080
Stocking Boys

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.940
We've got the new afternoon volumes.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.520
They're here!

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.000
We've still got two more 
carts of new volumes.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.910
Some re-stocks, too!

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.290
There's nowhere left to put them!

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.480
Maybe we should just put them 
out front in their boxes.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.390
Boss!

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.460
<b>Online outrage guaranteed!!</b>

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.460
Please get a grip!

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.550
We have a ton of boxes... What are they?

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.570
They're all new Kadokawa books.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:53.440
All of them?!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.310
In charge of KADOKAWA men's comics
 Gas Mask-senpai

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.000
And they all come with bonus material.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.310
Please and thank you.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.090
The BL books come with bonuses, too!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.960
And the novels come with flyers.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.460
Sorry, those BL books and novels
 are a partial shipment.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:14.820
<b>Partial shipment:</b> When books 
arrive a day later than scheduled

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.720
The rest will come tomorrow morning.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.150
Aiya...

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.770
Okay, I have to work at the counter, now.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.880
Crap, my new books arrived today.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:25.170
In charge of girls' comics
 Houtai-senpai

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.910
I didn't think they'd get here.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.480
That's a new thing to hope for.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:36.550
In charge of novels
 Koomote-san

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.880
My new books came partial.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.420
I'm supposed to be on break tomorrow...

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.340
I'm sorry, everyone tomorrow.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.550
What a tragedy.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.210
Honda.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.340
I'm packing the Kadokawa 
books with extras in them.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:43.150
In charge of Kou-D-sha
 Okitsune-senpai

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.150
Thank you.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:47.210
Man, do we really need this in our area?

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:51.430
In charge of BL
 Manager Armor

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:51.430
In charge of Sho-G-Kan
 Fullface-senpai

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:51.430
Pictures of Swords

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.160
Maybe we should ask if we can 
put them at the fine arts section.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.050
<i>All hands need to be on deck 
at the new books section.</i>

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:59.020
<i>We all need to cross each 
others' turf and help out.</i>

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:03.960
<i>I have to finish my books and start preparing
 tomorrow's stock of comic magazines.</i>

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.440
<b>Tower of Comic Magazine Boxes</b>

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.490
Okay, done packing the Kadokawa books.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:07.740
Huh?! Already?!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.710
The game guide books are done, too.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.100
The negotiation's ongoing, though.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.350
I think we should sell them 
at the fine arts section, too.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.250
Wait, so the new books are done?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.600
Some of them were partial.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.360
Um, I'm sorry...

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.690
Have you seen my new books?

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:27.760
Oh, dear.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.740
Are you sure those weren't partial, too?

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.210
Did you get any requests?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:36.090
Actually, I was expecting them today, 
so something feels amiss.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.670
Oh, hang on.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:38.960
Isn't this it?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:42.880
In charge of 4-koma and subculture
 Kamibukuro-senpai

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.800
It was off to the side.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.880
Whoa, I never noticed.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.190
Thanks, Kamibukuro-senpai.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.590
I'll bring it over now.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.050
Oh, it's okay. It's heavy, so I'll take it.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.090
<b>Crack</b>

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.090
Kamibukuro-senpai's spine!

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.700
Oh, don't be so pathetic, Kami-chan.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:56.550
I'll take it.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:58.120
Move, move.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.930
<b>Crunch</b>

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.720
Houtai-senpai's back, too!

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.170
We warned them.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.200
Honda-san's books are super heavy.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:08.480
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.870
<i>My books are mostly foreign comics.</i>

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.870
In charge of foreign comics and art books
 Honda

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:22.150
<b>Web Slinging Man</b>

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:22.150
<b>Raging Spy Gentleman</b>

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:22.150
<b>Superb Man</b>

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:17.220
<i>Unlike Japanese manga, they're huge, 
they use extremely high-quality paper,</i>

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:22.150
<b>Huge</b>

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:22.150
<b>Good paper</b>

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.160
<i>and, unbelievably, they're full color.</i>

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:22.150
<b>Color</b>

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.150
<i>So they're heavy as </i>hell<i>.</i>

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.960
<i>I can hold ordinary books with my 
jaw, but American comics? Nope.</i>

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:29.050
Japanese comics

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:29.050
Foreign comics

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.760
<i>No way.</i>

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.540
<i>My arms will fall off.</i>

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.330
Honda-san, want to use the two-tier cart?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:35.430
<b>Super useful!</b>

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.440
That must be heavy.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.180
Thank you.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.430
Not today, though.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.200
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.670
<b>Super busy</b>

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.470
Sorry, I guess you'd run 
the customers over, huh?

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.400
No, it's fine. Yeah...

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.090
All right, everyone, let's 
do tomorrow's new books!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.720
Wakey wakey, even if your back hurts.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.910
Time for the comic magazines.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:51.740
My back...

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.010
It hurts...

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.230
American comics scare me.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.480
I'll help as soon as I set 
the American comics up.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:58.820
Pardon me!

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.520
Pardon me!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.490
Pardon m—

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.220
<i>By the way, everyone. Have you noticed?</i>

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.730
<i>There's a task that I haven't even
 started since this morning.</i>

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:12.120
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:13.730
I'm back.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.220
I'll work on the comic magazines.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.390
Don't worry.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.220
But I still have to put 
in the papers and such.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:19.850
Yeah!

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.390
Let's leave the new books to them.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:22.880
Meanwhile, the two of us have to...

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:25.160
pack the shelves like our
 lives depend on it!

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.120
I forgot about that!

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:30.280
I told you in the beginning.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.930
We won't be able to pack the shelves.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.500
I'll do it tomorrow.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:38.220
She <i>did</i> actually say that!

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.870
Man, my back hurts.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:42.980
<b>Man, my
 back hurts</b>

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:42.630
We forgot to pack the shelves because of all 
the new book prep and more new book prep.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:47.430
<i>For there to be so many in the back 
means there are no books up front!</i>

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:51.150
<i>Plenty in stock but none on display 
means a surge of customer inquiries,</i>

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.530
<i>which means call bell hell.</i>

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.670
<i>Oh, god!</i>

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:56.610
<i>But wait...</i>

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.000
<i>Could it already be...</i>

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.380
<b>Closing Time</b>

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.690
When did that happen?! Dammit!

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:09.620
<b>Overtime confirmed!!</b>

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.050
Let's finish this like 
our lives depend on it!

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.620
Hey! Don't work too much overtime!

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.020
Come on!

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:13.610
** Bookstore

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.860
<b>Books, Written Instructions, and Me</b>

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:24.570
<b>I'm heading out</b>

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:24.330
<i>Kamibukuro-senpai went on vacation, 
and left us with written instructions.</i>

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.550
I'm heading out.

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:31.840
<b>New subculture & 4-koma books</b>

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:31.840
<b>Wham</b>

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.030
I thought it'd be a lot more rough.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.580
This is the work of someone 
who knows what they're doing.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:39.950
In charge of game guide books
 Rabbit Head-chan

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:37.170
I honestly don't know how to sort or 
display subculture and 4-koma books,

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.640
so this is helpful.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:39.420
Yeah.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:49.260
In charge of Shu-E-sha
 Lantern-senpai

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:43.890
And when it comes to large publishers...

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:49.260
<b>New Shu-E-sha books 
We get a ton of <i>One **ece</i>, so just 
make sure they're in the store. -Lantern</b>

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:48.630
We get a ton of <i>One **ece</i>, so just 
make sure they're in the store.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:53.010
All right, let's do what we can with 
the subculture books while Senpai's gone.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:53.940
Okay.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.930
One week later

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.930
I'm home!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:02.470
<b>Gifts</b>

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:02.470
Guys, thanks for putting out 
the new subculture books!

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:09.700
Subculture

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.850
Wait, there's nothing there.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:04.660
Why not?

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:09.180
We got almost no books while you were away.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.980
Kami-chan.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.020
<b>New subculture books</b>

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.300
We just now got the new books.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.860
<i>Don't give up, Senpai...</i>

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.890
<b>Go! Azarashi-san</b>

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.130
Hey, everyone.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.610
Are you enjoying <i>Skull-face 
Bookseller Honda-san</i>?

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:40.080
The original manga was based on the real 
experiences of former bookseller Honda-san.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:41.440
I see.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:44.640
The back of a bookstore 
can be pretty mysterious,

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.460
but hopefully this manga 
makes things clearer.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:52.910
<i>You'd expect no less from a bookseller 
than to give recommendations so naturally.</i>

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.840
By the way, Honda-san...

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.620
You scared me!

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.570
Please call me "Azarashi" in your books.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:02.640
<i>This is my editor, Azarashi-san.</i>

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.990
Editor Azarashi-san

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:07.640
<i>An assigned editor gives advice 
to make manga more interesting,</i>

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.370
Yeah, this is funny!

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.120
<i>hears me out when I need 
to talk, and cheers me up.</i>

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:11.000
Go, go Honda!

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:12.220
<i>They're very valuable to have around.</i>

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.720
You can do it, Honda!

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:16.030
I was hoping to draw the skeleton cuter.

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:17.280
Oh, it's okay.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.750
I don't expect you to draw anything cute.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.010
<b>No expectation</b>

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:25.360
I think the skeleton's the most hilarious—I mean, 
likable—when he's working really hard.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:30.060
<i>I'm lucky I was met with someone 
with such an open mind.</i>
